# `Symbol.for("text")` finds the one symbol that is registered under the text, wherever the call stands and however often it runs. The front end names the field of `[kState]: ..` by the text,
# Link lets the symbol go along with its key as it does for a symbol that is made once, and an access under it is an access under a name. A text that nobody knows stays a call and an access under a key.
# RUN: link accesses mechanisms=all
